blem  in their neighborhood well I think there  are three things we want to achieve  first is a major advance in terms of  funds for the UN programs and this is so  important this is food for refugees it's  shelter for refugees it's making sure  that in those refugee camps and in the  neighboring countries people can be  properly looked after and I want us to  do a lot better this year than last year  and I think we will second is education  let's make sure that we don't have  refugee children in the region or else  we're not in school by the end of the  next academic year I think that's  absolutely vital  third and creatively you were trying to  help those people in the region who  would like to stay there and work and  provide for their families because of  course people's first choice would be to  go back to Syria they can't do that at  the moment their second choice is  probably to stay in the region but to  provide for their children that are  helping them to do that with more work  permits is something we're looking at

